Two possible mirror setups were investigated: 1) the mirrors composing the SCE have a perfect alignment, i.e. there are no errors in its parabolic shape; and 2) the mirrors are subject to minor displacements out of their optimal position. In the second setup the SCE is composed of 28 slightly distorted mirrors (Figure \ref{fig:picture_setup}) to consider possible misalignments in the SCE caused by the ageing of the components, and the operation of the solar field.


