 \section{Conclusion}

 In this paper, we have obtained some optimized extension of the 3/4-majority rule and the MOT which provides scalable and efficient space reduction techniques for many instances of the Kemeny problem. Experimental results show in particular that $(\alpha, \beta)$-MOT  and $(\alpha, \beta)$-majority are rather complementary and their iterated combination performs particularly well and significantly boosts the individual performance of each of these majority rules. 











