\section{Learning and Gradient Descent}\label{sec:learning}

In this section, we flesh out the reaction network scheme for the learning (backpropagation) part of the SVM through gradient descent. In particular, this will implement Equations~\ref{eq:mis_update} and~\ref{eq:no_mis_update}. We describe it in the following four steps:

\textbf{Step 1:}


In this step, we calculate the quantity $\eta \cdot \lambda \cdot [W_i]$ from Equation~\ref{eq:mis_update} and~\ref{eq:no_mis_update}. In particular, each weight $W_i$ is multiplied by the learning parameter $\eta$ and the regularization parameter $\lambda$. This update is stored in $WA_i$ and is applied to the weight regardless of whether the outcome is correct or incorrect
\begin{eqnarray}
\begin{split}
O_4 + \eta + \lambda + W_1 &\rightarrow O_4 + \eta + \lambda + W_1 + WA_1 \\
WA_1 + O_4 &\rightarrow O_4\\
O_4 + \eta + \lambda + W_2 &\rightarrow O_4 + \eta + \lambda + W_2 + WA_2 \\
WA_2 + O_4 &\rightarrow O_4\\
\vdots &\\
O_4 + \eta + \lambda + W_n &\rightarrow O_4 + \eta + \lambda + W_n + WA_n \\
WA_n + O_4 &\rightarrow O_4\\
\end{split}
\end{eqnarray}


The dynamical system corresponding to this network is 
\begin{eqnarray}
\frac{d[WA_i]}{dt} = \eta \lambda [W_i] [O_4] - [WA_i] [O_4]
\end{eqnarray}

At steady state, we get $[WA_i^{ss}] = \eta \cdot \lambda \cdot [W_i(0)]$.


\textbf{Step 2:}


Here, we handle conditional weight updates. In particular, we calculate the quantity $\eta \cdot [K_{gtQ}] \cdot [X_i] \cdot [Y]$ and $\eta \cdot [K_{gtQ}] \cdot [Y]$ . If the outcome is incorrect, we use $K_{gtQ}$ as a catalyst with unit concentration, storing the former product in $XY_i$ and latter in $BY$. If the outcome is correct, $K_{gtQ}$ is zero, preventing any weight update.

\begin{eqnarray}
\begin{split}
O_4 + \eta + Y + X_1 + K_{gtQ} &\rightarrow O_4 + \eta + Y + X_1 + XY_1 + K_{gtQ} \\
XY_1 + O_4 &\rightarrow O_4 \\
\vdots & \\
O_4 + \eta + Y + X_n + K_{gtQ} &\rightarrow O_4 + \eta + Y + X_n + XY_n + K_{gtQ} \\
XY_n + O_4 &\rightarrow O_4 \\
O_4 + \eta + Y  + K_{gtQ} &\rightarrow O_4 + \eta + Y + BY + K_{gtQ} \\
BY + O_4 &\rightarrow O_4 \\
\end{split}
\end{eqnarray}

The dynamical system corresponding to this network is 
\begin{eqnarray}
\frac{d[XY_i]}{dt} = \eta [K_{gtQ}] [X_i] [Y] [O_4] - [XY_i][O_4]
\end{eqnarray}
\& for bias
\begin{eqnarray}
\frac{d[BY]}{dt} = \eta [K_{gtQ}]  [Y] [O_4] - [BY][O_4]
\end{eqnarray}

At steady state, we get $[XY_i^{ss}] = \eta \cdot [K_{gtQ}] \cdot [X_i] \cdot [Y]$ and $[BY^{ss}] = \eta \cdot [K_{gtQ}] \cdot [Y]$.


\textbf{Step 3:}
Note that in both equations~\ref{eq:mis_update} and~\ref{eq:no_mis_update}, the term $\eta \cdot \lambda \cdot [W_i]$ is always subtracted from the weights irrespective of misclassifications. We will implement this update in the current step. In particular, 
we subtract the always-updated value ($WA_i$) from the original weight ($W_i$) and store the result in $WD_i$.

\begin{eqnarray}
\begin{split}
W_i + O_5 &\rightarrow O_5 + W_i + WD_i \\
WA_i + O_5 &\rightarrow O_5 + WA_i + H \\
WD_i +  O_5 &\rightarrow O_5 \\
WD_i + H + O_5 &\rightarrow O_5 \\
\end{split}
\end{eqnarray}

The dynamical system corresponding to this network is 
\begin{eqnarray}
\frac{d[WD_i]}{dt} = [W_i] [O_5] - [WD_i][O_5] - [WD_i] [H] [O_5]
\end{eqnarray}
\&
\begin{eqnarray}
\frac{d[H]}{dt} = [WA_i] [O_5] - [WD_i] [H] [O_5]
\end{eqnarray}

At steady state, we get $[H^{ss}] = [WA_i] / [WD_i]$ and $[WD_i^{ss}] = [W_i] - [WA_i] $.

We also store the sum of the old bias \textit{b} and the update to the bias BY in a new variable BT.
\begin{eqnarray}
\begin{split}
b + O_5 &\rightarrow O_5 + b + BT \\
BY + O_5 &\rightarrow O_5 + BY + BT \\
BT +  O_5 &\rightarrow O_5 \\
\end{split}
\end{eqnarray}

The dynamical system corresponding to this network is 
\begin{eqnarray}
\frac{d[BT]}{dt} = [b] [O_5] + [BY][O_5] - [BT] [O_5]
\end{eqnarray}

At steady state, we get $[BT^{ss}] = [b] + [BY] $.

\textbf{Step 4:}


Finally, we apply the conditional weight update ($XY_j$) to $WD_i$, loading it into $W_i$, thus completing the final weight update. 

\begin{eqnarray}
\begin{split}
WD_i + O_6 &\rightarrow WD_i + O_6 + W_i \\
XY_i + O_6 &\rightarrow XY_i + O_6 + W_i \\
BT + O_6 &\rightarrow BT + O_6 + b  \\
W_i + O_6 &\rightarrow O_6 \\
b + O_6 &\rightarrow O_6 \\
\end{split}
\end{eqnarray}

The dynamical system corresponding to this network is 
\begin{eqnarray}
\frac{dW_i}{dt} = [WD_i][O_6] + [XY_i][O_6] - [W_i][O_6]
\end{eqnarray}
and for bias
\begin{eqnarray}
\frac{db}{dt} = [BT][O_6] - [b][O_6]
\end{eqnarray}

At steady state, we get $[W_i^{ss}] = [WD_i] + [X][Y] $  and $[b^{ss}] = [BT]$.

As a consequence, we have implemented Equations~\ref{eq:mis_update} and~\ref{eq:no_mis_update} and the backpropagation module is complete.

