We also conducted the other simulation experiments to see the dynamics of error-correction where we input noise to each cell with a certain probability during 500 time steps and remove the noise input after 500 steps. Fig. \ref{fig:pattern} shows the examples of  error correction for each error rate. Here, a black dot represents a damaged cell site, and a gray dot represents a cell with Flag1 = 1, broadly implying that an error was detected in the cell’s state or in the neighboring cells.

