As we can see from the simulation with an error rate of 0.05 (Fig. \ref{fig:pattern}A), for small errors, the error correction process is almost always completed in 1 step by the majority vote with the neighbors.The information of Flag1 = 1 propagates to the cell on the left side, and if there is no inconsistency at the border of colony, the wave of Flag1 = 1 stops, and the original state will be completely restored.

