We can use this explicit solution to compute the equilibrium cost. We report the result in terms of additional simplifying constants $\psi,\xi, \mathfrak{p}$, and $\mathfrak{h}_j$ ($j=1,\dots,5$) whose definitions are provided in Table \ref{tab:constants}.

\begin{corollary}\label{cor:eq.cost.term.pen}
