\begin{definition}\label{ratiodef}
If $A, B, C$ are three points on a line $\ell^{OI}$ (collinear) in Desargues affine plane, then we define their \textbf{ratio} to be a point $R \in \ell^{OI}$, such that:
\[
(B-C)\cdot R=A-C, \quad \mbox{concisely}\quad R=(B-C)^{-1}(A-C),
\]
and we mark this with  $r(A,B;C)= (B-C)^{-1}(A-C)$.
\end{definition}
