\begin{abstract}
    We establish the minimal model program (MMP) for generalized foliated threefolds $(X, \mathcal{F}, B, \mathbf{M})$ of rank 1, extending the result of Cascini and Spicer in \cite{CS20}. As an application of the generalized foliated MMP, we prove a base-point-free theorem for foliated triples on threefolds. We also prove the ACC for log canonical thresholds for generalized foliated threefolds of rank 1.
\end{abstract}

