\begin{corollary}\label{coro:singinvcurve}
    Let $X$ be a $\Q$-factorial normal variety and $(X, \cF, B, \bM)$ be a rank 1 gfq. Let $C \subset \Sing ^+ \cF$ be a curve and suppose that $(X, \cF, B, \bM)$ is lc at the generic point of $C$. Then $(K_\cF + B + \bM_X) \cdot C \geq 0$.
