    \end{align*}
    If $\bN^{L_i}_{L_i^\nu} \neq 0$ for all $i$, then by Lemma \ref{lemma:finiteset}, there exists $\nu_i'\in I$, occurring as a coefficient of $\bN^{L_i}_{L_i^\nu}$, such that $t_i\nu_i'$ belongs to a finite set independent of $i$, which contradicts to the the choice of $t_i$. Thus we may assume that $\bN^{L_i}_{L_i^\nu} = 0$ for all $i$.

